--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -125,6 +125,74 @@ cargo run --release -- \
 
 ## Configuration
 
+### Router middleware
+
+Router-native middleware is opt-in through repeatable `--middleware` options.
+For OpenAI-compatible agent requests, enable `agent_hint_affinity` to copy
+`agent_hint.session_id` into `session_params.session_id` before routing:
+
+Build and invoke the Rust release binary directly:
+
+```bash
+cd agentrouter
+cargo build --release
+
+./target/release/vllm-router \
+    --worker-urls http://localhost:8080 http://localhost:8081 \
+    --policy cache_aware \
+    --middleware agent_hint_affinity
+```
+
+Or install the Python package, whose console command forwards the same option
+through PyO3 to the Rust Router:
+
+```bash
+cd agentrouter
+python -m pip install -e .
+
+vllm-router \
+    --worker-urls http://localhost:8080 http://localhost:8081 \
+    --policy cache_aware \
+    --middleware agent_hint_affinity
+```
+
+For one vLLM endpoint exposing multiple intra-node DP ranks, the Router DP size
+must match vLLM's `--data-parallel-size`:
+
+```bash
+./target/release/vllm-router \
+    --worker-urls http://localhost:8080 \
+    --intra-node-data-parallel-size 4 \
+    --policy cache_aware \
+    --chat-routing-key-mode session-id-full-history-fallback \
+    --middleware agent_hint_affinity
+```
+
+The middleware applies only to `/v1/chat/completions`. Middleware names select
+built-in Rust implementations; Python ASGI import paths are not loaded by the
+Rust Router.
+
+To retain the same session affinity and also translate
+`agent_hint.cache_control.msg_offset` into token and block coordinates, use the
+`agent_hint_token_offsets` middleware:
+
+```bash
+./target/release/vllm-router \
+    --worker-urls http://localhost:8080 \
+    --policy cache_aware \
+    --middleware agent_hint_token_offsets \
+    --agent-hint-tokenizer /models/Qwen/tokenizer.json \
+    --agent-hint-chat-template /models/Qwen/chat_template.jinja \
+    --agent-hint-block-size 128
+```
+
+The tokenizer, chat template, and block size must match the backend. The Router
+loads the tokenizer once at startup, recalculates client-provided derived
+offsets, and forwards `token_offset`, `block_offset`, and
+`intra_block_offset`. It does not execute cache offload, prefetch, or eviction;
+the backend must consume those fields. `agent_hint_affinity` and
+`agent_hint_token_offsets` are mutually exclusive.
+
 ### Authentication
 
 Enable bearer-token validation by listing validation URLs (comma-separated) in `.env` via `API_KEY_VALIDATION_URLS` or passing `--api-key-validation-urls`.
